From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: karol <karolprzybylak1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:57:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Send TX_ACK without JSON when the downlink was accepted

For an accepted downlink the forwarder sent {"txpk_ack":{"error":""}}.
An empty string is not one of the protocol's "error" values; Semtech's
packet forwarders send no JSON at all when there is nothing to report,
and PROTOCOL.TXT (section 5.5) defines a TX_ACK without JSON as "no
error occurred".

The Things Stack maps every "error" value other than "NONE" to
UNKNOWN_ERROR, so each downlink through this forwarder was shown as
ns.down.transmission.fail although the gateway sent it, and the network
server repeated its MAC commands after every uplink. ChirpStack accepts
both forms, so nothing changes there.

Success is still the empty string internally, so the TX_ACK_OK metric
stays as it is.

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/chirpstack/chirpstack-udp-forwarder/pull/36]
---
 src/structs.rs | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/structs.rs b/src/structs.rs
index c2003cc..558d260 100644
--- a/src/structs.rs
+++ b/src/structs.rs
@@ -640,8 +640,13 @@ impl TxAck {
         b.push(0x05);
         b.append(&mut self.gateway_id.to_vec());
 
-        let mut j = serde_json::to_vec(&self.payload).unwrap();
-        b.append(&mut j);
+        // No JSON when there is nothing to report: the Semtech UDP protocol treats a TX_ACK
+        // without payload as success. An empty "error" string is not a valid value (The Things
+        // Stack reports it as UNKNOWN_ERROR).
+        if !self.payload.txpk_ack.error.is_empty() {
+            let mut j = serde_json::to_vec(&self.payload).unwrap();
+            b.append(&mut j);
+        }
 
         b
     }
@@ -1169,4 +1174,20 @@ mod tests {
             r#"{"txpk_ack":{"error":"TOO_LATE"}}"#,
         );
     }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn test_tx_ack_ok() {
+        let tx_ack = TxAck {
+            random_token: 123,
+            gateway_id: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8],
+            payload: TxAckPayload {
+                txpk_ack: TxAckPayloadError {
+                    error: "".to_string(),
+                },
+            },
+        };
+
+        let b = tx_ack.to_bytes();
+        assert_eq!(b, vec![2, 0, 123, 5, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]);
+    }
 }
